# Writer 11 (tally 2.1, R-1). L §3.6 The shares: "The shares of one arrival sum to exactly 1, or the arrival is refused
# (RUN-LABEL)"; a part never goes below zero (L §3.6: "An owned or batched kind is min 0 ..., so a part never goes below
# zero"). 2.1-F4: "The shares of one arrival are each at least 0 and sum to exactly 1, or the arrival is refused
# (RUN-LABEL ...)"; L §8.4 `the share of <party> in <movement>'s arrival at <place> is below 0`. Shares 2 and -1.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind persons: parties
kind couples: parties
kind savings: place PLN min 0
  owned by arrive
  step minor(PLN)
  takes k for w order if k.owner == ania then 0 else 1
input hi: num
input lo: num
place konto: savings lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
place shop: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input a1_day: date
input a1_amt: money PLN
def arrive[m in events, p in parties]: num at m.day
  rule base = if p == ania then hi else if p == tomek then lo else 0
move a1: transfers
  on a1_day
  leg cash from world to konto amount a1_amt
ask q: bal(konto, 2026-03-31), bal(konto, 2026-03-31) of ania

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  persons + [ania] lives 1980-01-01..
  persons + [tomek] lives 1981-01-01..
  couples + [ania_tomek] lives 2010-06-01..
  opening[konto] = 0 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
  a1_day = 2026-02-01
  a1_amt = 100.00 PLN
  hi = 2
  lo = -1
=== expect
q: (refused: RUN-LABEL the share of tomek in a1's arrival at konto is below 0, refused: RUN-LABEL the share of tomek in a1's arrival at konto is below 0)
  cut 2026-01-01
